{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked (in Chinese) to complete the full design in the assigned Figma file https://www.figma.com/design/w8cdABfIOMXOTNZPXNSZhR/ (fileKey `w8cdABfIOMXOTNZPXNSZhR`): read the task in 「00 · Start Here」, follow the visual spec in 「01 · Foundations」, reuse components from 「02 · Components」, use assets from 「04 · Media」, and deliver the complete design into 「03 · Workspace」.\n\n   Harness-level requirements (still in force): confirm the account via whoami before writing (must be gaoyongyong@tetras.ai); use only the assigned file; read reference pages before writing; create all work inside the workspace page (create it if missing) and preserve existing reference pages; do not create another Figma file or switch accounts/teams; build in sections and check results before continuing; add prototype interactions after the relevant screens exist; inspect screenshots of all required screens and fix visible problems; finish with the file URL, the 03 · Workspace page ID, the screen IDs, prototype work completed, and remaining limitations; do not claim completion for unfinished work; before every tool call emit a visible summary prefixed exactly `Reasoning summary:`, and the final response must start with `Reasoning summary: ...` then `Final answer:`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma MCP tools: `whoami`, `get_metadata` (nodeId required for subtree), `use_figma` (JavaScript against the Figma Plugin API), `get_screenshot`.\n   - Figma Plugin API: `figma.setCurrentPageAsync`, `figma.getNodeByIdAsync`, `node.clone()`, `figma.createFrame()`, `figma.loadFontAsync`, autolayout props (`layoutMode`, padding, itemSpacing), fills/strokes/effects, cornerRadius.\n   - Design system: brand red #EF2A39 and dark brown #3C2F2F fixed; Lobster only for the Foodgo wordmark (supplied vector components), Roboto for all UI text; base viewport 430 × 932; Home and Customize may scroll vertically.\n   - Fixed data/copy must be reproduced exactly (prices, ratings, times, chat order, \"26 minutes ago\" placement).\n   - Prototype reactions are required per the brief's link list.\n   - Note: the brief's handoff text says \"copy into your own new file,\" but the harness overrides this: delivery is the workspace inside the assigned copy. I am building in `w8cdABfIOMXOTNZPXNSZhR` → page 2006:2.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - Figma page `0:1` (00 · Start Here) — read for the assignment. Key fixed content:\n     - 11 exact frame names: `01_Splash · 02_Home · 03_Product_Cheeseburger · 04_Product_Veggie · 05_Product_Chicken · 06_Product_Fried_Chicken · 07_Customize · 08_Payment · 09_Payment_Success_Overlay · 10_Profile · 11_Support_Chat`.\n     - Menu data: Cheeseburger · Wendy's Burger · 4.9 · 26 mins · $8.24 (portion 1 = $8.24); Hamburger · Veggie Burger · 4.8 · 14 mins · $9.99 (portion 1); Hamburger · Chicken Burger · 4.6 · 42 mins · $6.24 (portion 2 = $12.48); Hamburger · Fried Chicken Burger · 4.5 · 14 mins · $6.75 (portion 4 = $27.00).\n     - Customize: added add-ons = Tomato, Cheese, Fries; copy \"Customize Your Burger to Your Tastes. Ultimate Experience\"; Total = 2 × $8.24 = $16.48.\n     - Payment: Order $16.48, Taxes $0.30, Delivery fees $1.50, Total $18.28, ETA 15–30 mins; Credit card (Mastercard, 5105 **** **** 0505) selected, Debit card (Visa, 3566 **** **** 0505) unselected; \"Save card details for future payments\" on.\n     - Profile: Sophia Patel, sophiapatel@gmail.com, 123 Main St, Apartment 4A, New York, NY; password masked+locked; Edit Profile, Log out, Order history, Payment Details, settings.\n     - Chat (7 items): A \"Hi, how can I help you